# Project rules / knowledge

## What this is
- solar-ctl: RPi-based controller for a **Deye inverter** (modbus), publishing to
  Home Assistant energy. Display: 2.79" NV3007 TFT.
- `fw/` — Yocto **kas** firmware build (this is the active part).
- `inv_ctl/` — empty for now; the inverter-controller app. Will be added to the
  image as an `inv-ctl` recipe (placeholder comment in `solar-ctl-image.bb`).
- Target board: **Raspberry Pi Zero W** (`machine: raspberrypi0-wifi`).

## Firmware build (fw/)
- Build with `kas build fw/kas-rpi0.yml` from the repo root (tested with kas 5.5).
- Release: Yocto **wrynose**. No poky: standalone oe-core + our distro conf
  `fw/conf/distro/solar-ctl.conf` (`TCLIBC=musl`, `INIT_MANAGER=systemd`,
  trimmed `DISTRO_FEATURES_DEFAULTS`).
- Layer refs: **branch mode** while pre-production (decided 2026-09): the kas
  file tracks branch tips (`wrynose`; bitbake `"2.18"` — bitbake has no
  wrynose branch and oe-core's sanity checker hard-requires 2.18). kas's
  "branch without commit is unsafe" warnings are expected/accepted. To
  freeze exact refs: `kas lock fw/kas-rpi0.yml` writes
  `fw/kas-rpi0.lock.yml`, which kas auto-applies to every build while it
  exists (update = re-run lock; floating again = delete it) — commit the
  lock file with a release tag. (The old `fw/kas-baseline.yml` manual pin
  copy was removed 2026-09 — it duplicated `kas-rpi0.yml`; the
  "last verified good" commits below are the reference.) **Re-pin `commit:` in
  `fw/kas-rpi0.yml` before tagging the first release.** Last verified good:
  oe-core `883075157987ca300af59185b903d6d1977234c3`,
  meta-raspberrypi `f62c67921474370829d24a4fa01ef88543f3906b`,
  bitbake `f0df79b6b56f6a69067adf974978d9405077f246`,
  meta-oe `14282a02be9c74a1276a7cda7d6c89e054699a11`.
- Use **GitHub mirrors**; `git.yoctoproject.org` is unreachable here (Cloudflare 403):
  use `github.com/openembedded/openembedded-core`, `openembedded/bitbake`,
  `agherzan/meta-raspberrypi`.
- The `solar-ctl` repo entry in the kas file deliberately has **no `url`**: kas
  builds from the working tree, don't "fix" it by adding a url.
- `layers/`, `build/`, `kas-build.log` are generated by kas — gitignored, never edit.
- CI cache (firmware.yml): sstate only (`build/sstate-cache`, ~1.3 GB) with a
  `yocto-*` restore-keys fallback and `-<sha>` save suffix. Do NOT cache
  `build/downloads` (~9.5 GB, 8.4 GB of it `git2` clones): GitHub's cache
  quota is 10 GB/repo and the old downloads+sstate entry sat at 9.97 GiB —
  one kernel bump from silently failing to save. `fw/kas-ci.yml` was deleted
  2026-09: its `INHERIT:remove = "rm_work"` was based on confusing rm_work
  with rm_work_and_downloads — rm_work never touches downloads/sstate, so
  it did nothing for the cache, only kept tmp/work on the runner.
- `SOLAR_WIFI_SSID/PSK/COUNTRY` are declared in `fw/kas-rpi0.yml`
  (`env:` section, CHANGEME placeholders — kas exports them to bitbake via
  BB_ENV_PASSTHROUGH_ADDITIONS and OS env vars override them). The real
  values live ONLY in the gitignored `.zed/tasks.json` "Build FW" env block
  (`.zed` is in .gitignore — keep it that way while it holds the PSK) and are
  baked into the image as a root-only 0600 file — treat built images as
  secret and never publish them. **Never put real WiFi credentials in
  committed files**; a gitignored `.kas-wifi-local.yml` fragment
  (`kas build fw/kas-rpi0.yml:.kas-wifi-local.yml`) works too — its
  local.conf `=` assignments beat the environment. CI injects them from
  Actions secrets (`SOLAR_WIFI_*`) via a generated `.kas-wifi-ci.yml`
  fragment (gitignored). Repo is PUBLIC: only bake a lab/guest SSID, never
  the real home PSK, into CI artifacts/releases. CI has a guard step that
  fails the build if any of these secret-bearing files ever get tracked by
  git (firmware.yml "Guard against committed secret files").

## Yocto/wrynose recipe gotchas (learned the hard way)
- `S = "${WORKDIR}"` is rejected on wrynose — use `S = "${UNPACKDIR}"` and
  `${UNPACKDIR}/<file>` paths for `file://` SRC_URI files.
- A line whose first char is `}` inside a recipe shell/python function breaks
  bitbake's parser (e.g. a `network={...}` heredoc). Use template files + sed.
- `serial-console` is **not** a valid IMAGE_FEATURE on wrynose (it silently
  skips the image recipe). With systemd the serial getty comes automatically
  from `ENABLE_UART=1` + `SERIAL_CONSOLES` (systemd-serialgetty).
- musl + systemd builds fine but bitbake warns it is *experimental* upstream.
- meta-raspberrypi adds `kernel-modules` (= all ~1800 modules) and BT firmware
  to `MACHINE_EXTRA_RRECOMMENDS` on every rpi image; `solar-ctl-image.bb`
  removes them. When a kernel feature is needed, add the specific
  `kernel-module-*` package instead of re-enabling `kernel-modules`.
- `ENABLE_USB_ETH` does not exist; USB gadget mode is `ENABLE_DWC2_PERIPHERAL = "1"`.
- Keep the image minimal: base is `core-image-minimal` + targeted adds only;
  don't pull `packagegroup-core-basic`/`-full-cmdline` style groups.
- WiFi creds (see the build section above for the full policy): locally they
  come from the Zed task env / OS environment. kas only passes env vars that
  are DECLARED in the kas config `env:` section through to bitbake
  (BB_ENV_PASSTHROUGH_ADDITIONS) — arbitrary undeclared env vars are ignored
  (that was the trap with the original tasks.json env block before the
  `env:` section existed). CI uses the generated fragment instead.
- **Never use `rm_work_and_downloads`** (use plain `INHERIT += "rm_work"`):
  it puts DL_DIR under `tmp/work/<machine>/<PN>/downloads` and deletes it in
  do_rm_work — breaks recipes built target+native from one tarball (git,
  gettext: `tar: Cannot open` in do_unpack). Its leftover do_fetch sstate
  objects keep stale paths and poison the cache even after reverting; wipe
  `build/tmp` + `build/sstate-cache` if recovering.
- Licenses: `LICENSE_FLAGS_ACCEPTED = "synaptics-killswitch"` is required by
  linux-firmware-rpidistro; keep it set.

## Kernel / device-tree (learned 2026-09, display + RS485 work)
- Kernel trim: `DISABLE_VC4GRAPHICS = "1"` (kas local_conf_header) drops the
  vc4graphics machine feature, else meta-raspberrypi's `vc4graphics.cfg`
  re-enables DRM_VC4 on top of our fragment. Our fragment:
  `fw/recipes-kernel/linux/files/solar-ctl-slim.cfg` (kernel-yocto applies
  `file://*.cfg` from SRC_URI automatically; linux-raspberrypi DOES require
  linux-yocto.inc). Keep `CONFIG_DRM=y`+`DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION=y`+`DRM_PANEL_MIPI_DBI`.
- Custom DTBOs: drop `.dts` in `fw/recipes-kernel/linux/files/`, copy to
  `${S}/arch/arm/boot/dts/overlays/` in `do_configure:append` (bbappend),
  append to `RPI_KERNEL_DEVICETREE_OVERLAYS` **in kas local_conf_header**
  (not the bbappend — IMAGE_BOOT_FILES is evaluated in the image recipe,
  which never sees kernel-recipe appends). The overlay MUST also be
  registered in `arch/arm/boot/dts/overlays/Makefile`'s `dtbo-y` list
  (we do it via `0001-overlays-register-…patch`): kbuild gives "No rule
  to make target" for unregistered overlays even as explicit make
  targets. kbuild maps `x.dtbo` ← `x-overlay.dts` (scripts/Makefile.dtbs),
  so `nv3007-overlay.dts` registers as **`nv3007.dtbo`** (no `-overlay`
  suffix) — and kernel-yocto COMMITS SRC_URI patches onto the shared
  kernel-source branch: if a patch changes, `git reset --hard
  <SRCREV>` in work-shared kernel-source before rebuilding, or the old
  commit lingers. Validate offline with the built kernel's
  `scripts/dtc/dtc` + `gcc -E -nostdinc -I <kernel-source>/include -x
  assembler-with-cpp` (dtc alone fails on `#include <dt-bindings/...>`).
- NV3007 TFT (corrected 2026-09): the panel is a **2.79" TZT 142×428
  portrait** module, not a 240×320 ILI9341 — use the generic
  `panel-mipi-dbi` driver (`compatible = "panel-mipi-dbi-spi"`;
  `CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_MIPI_DBI=m` already in bcmrpi_defconfig). Mode comes
  from a `panel-timing` child node in the overlay (hactive/vactive +
  porches; blank/unspecified props = 0 is accepted). The controller init
  sequence is a **firmware file** `/lib/firmware/panel-mipi-dbi-spi.bin`
  (= compatible[0] + ".bin"; request_firmware, retried ~every 60s) — we
  do NOT ship it yet, so the panel stays dark until the vendor init code
  is baked in; never fabricate NV3007 register values. mipi-dbi has no
  DT `rotation`; rotate in software. `TINYDRM_ILI9341` is now disabled
  in the slim fragment. Modules: kernel-module-{panel-mipi-dbi,spi-bcm2835,gpio-backlight}.
- Zero W UART reality (corrected 2026-09): rpi DT names `uart0`=PL011
  (ttyAMA0), `uart1`=mini (ttyS0). On Zero W the PL011's default pads
  GPIO30–33 are wired to the onboard BCM43430 (NOT the header); the
  40-pin header's only UART pair is GPIO14/15, which **both** UARTs can
  reach — so console and native RS485 are mutually exclusive there.
  Default = mini console on 14/15; `solar-rs485` overlay moves PL011 to
  14/15 + RTS on GPIO17 (cts**rts**_gpio16 group = CTS16/RTS17, ALT3)
  and disables uart1. amba-pl011 has real RS485 support; PL011 is =y in
  bcmrpi_defconfig (no module pkg needed). `uart1` overlay ≠ PL011!
- RS485 direction: `rs485ctl` recipe (fw/recipes-support/rs485ctl) wraps
  TIOCSRS485 (enable/invert/delays) — busybox has no applet for this.
- Module pkg names are derived from the module .o name: gpio_backlight.c
  → package `kernel-module-gpio-backlight` (hyphens, not underscores);
  verify in `build/tmp/pkgdata/*/runtime/` (survives rm_work).
- `build/tmp/work-shared/raspberrypi0-wifi/kernel-source` survives rm_work
  — grep defconfigs/board DTS/overlays there instead of unpacking anything.

## A/B OTA / SWUpdate (in design — full record in fw/docs/swupdate-ota.md)
- Target: A/B **squashfs-xz** read-only roots + `/etc` overlay + ext4 `/data`;
  slot switch by **RPi firmware** (no U-Boot). Design only, nothing built yet.
- `overlayfs-etc.bbclass` (oe-core) is the `/etc` mechanism, BUT its default
  `OVERLAYFS_ETC_CREATE_MOUNT_DIRS=1` does `mount -o remount,rw /` — on a
  squashfs root that can never work. Set it to `0` and pre-create `/data`.
  Also conflicts with IMAGE_FEATURES `package-management`.
- `overlayfs.bbclass` (for `/var`) requires the **`overlayfs` DISTRO_FEATURE,
  which is NOT in `DISTRO_FEATURES_DEFAULTS`** in fw/conf/distro/solar-ctl.conf
  — must be added (+ kernel `CONFIG_OVERLAY_FS`). It refuses `/etc` by design.
  `/var/volatile` for RO rootfs is initscripts-only → systemd never runs it.
- Slot switching: `tryboot` is the mechanism — firmware sets a one-shot flag,
  clears it, and loads `tryboot.txt` **instead of** `config.txt`. Kernel side
  verified (`drivers/firmware/raspberrypi.c` parses `reboot="0 tryboot"` →
  `RPI_FIRMWARE_SET_REBOOT_FLAGS`, binds on bcm2835-firmware). Arm with
  `echo '0 tryboot' > /run/systemd/reboot-param && systemctl reboot` (systemd>=254).
  `autoboot.txt`/`tryboot_a_b` exists but legacy start.elf support is untested.
  Nothing decrements a boot counter (tryboot is consumed pre-kernel) → rely on
  `panic=N` + per-slot `slot=A|B` cmdline token, not a bootcount.
- meta-swupdate has a `wrynose` branch; configured by **its own Kconfig**
  merged over `recipes-support/swupdate/swupdate/defconfig` (no PACKAGECONFIG).
  Shipped defconfig is wrong for us: `CONFIG_UBOOT=y` (we have no U-Boot),
  `SURICATTA`/`CURL`/`SIGNED_IMAGES`/`HASH_VERIFY` all off. Hawkbit = just
  `CONFIG_SURICATTA=y` (+CURL_SSL) — a config, not a protocol to implement.
  No RPi bootloader handler exists (`none/ebg/uboot/grub/cboot` only) → set
  `bootloader_transaction_marker=false; bootloader_state_marker=false;` and
  switch slots ourselves; no `dual_copy` property — standby slot is our job.
  `installed-directly=true` is **mandatory on 512 MB** (else it extracts to
  tmpfs /tmp). `swupdate-www/-client/-ipc/-lua` are packages of `swupdate`.
- **`wic` moved OUT of oe-core** (verified 2026-09-23: no `scripts/lib/wic`
  on wrynose or master). It is a standalone project consumed as a recipe:
  `meta/recipes-support/wic/wic_0.3.1.bb` → `git://git.yoctoproject.org/wic.git`
  tag v0.3.1, built as `wic-native`. Consequences: canned wks now live in
  **`<layer>/files/wic/`** (so ours goes in `fw/files/wic/`); `image_types_wic`
  gained an `IMAGER=direct` abstraction; plugin source (rawcopy) is only
  greppable locally in `build/downloads/git2/git.yoctoproject.org.wic.git`.
  Cloudflare still 403s the cgit **web** UI — if `wic-native` ever fails to
  fetch, mirror wic.git to GitHub and override SRC_URI in a bbappend.
- Hazards: `/etc` overlay upper is **shared by both slots and survives
  rollback** (factory reset = wipe the upper dir; app config belongs in
  `/data`); **never OTA `bootcode.bin`/`start.elf`** (corrupt GPU firmware =
  truck roll); keep p1 FAT writes rare; MSDOS table + ext4 **fs labels**
  (`/dev/disk/by-label/`), since `by-partlabel` needs GPT.
- Bootloader version check: `bitbake -e rpi-bootfiles | grep -E
  '^(PV|SRCREV|RPIFW_DATE)='` (PV=`${RPIFW_DATE}`), or the
  `rpi-bootfiles-<PV>.stamp` in the deploy dir; `vcgencmd version` needs
  libraspberrypi-bin (not installed). Bench probe: `fw/tools/ota-probe.sh`.

## Editor on target
- Use **busybox `vi`** — decided 2026-09 after evaluating classic nvi 1.81.6:
  it fails to build on wrynose's GCC (2003-era code calls `conv_init`/`conv_enc`
  with no prototypes anywhere in the tarball; implicit decls are hard errors
  since GCC 14). Don't retry nvi without backporting the missing prototypes
  (plus stale bundled config.sub — needs gnu-config copy). Also needs db
  compat185 bbappend for `dbopen()`. Not worth it for a Zero W image.

## Device facts
- Zero W WiFi/BT chip: BCM43430 (firmware `linux-firmware-rpidistro-bcm43430`
  comes from the machine conf; driver `brcmfmac` installed in the image).
- Console: UART 115200 8N1; image has dropbear but **root has no password**
  by default (set via serial `passwd`, or lab-only `empty-root-password`).
- SSH policy: `/etc/default/dropbear` (our `dropbear.default` via the
  bbappend) sets `DROPBEAR_EXTRA_ARGS="-s"` — password logins disabled,
  root key login allowed. **dropbear `-B` means "allow blank password
  logins", NOT "reject passwords"** — never use it for key-only policy
  (with the lab `empty-root-password` feature, older dropbear would then
  accept a blank root password over SSH; 2025.89 happens to reject blank
  passwords anyway, but that is an accident, not the mechanism).
- Image artifact: `build/tmp/deploy/images/raspberrypi0-wifi/*.wic.bz2`;
  flash with `bmaptool copy` to the raw SD device.
